// ===========================================================================
// TON PRIMES — the LP SINK. LOCKED DEPTH, AND NOTHING ELSE.
// CONCEPT.md §3.4, §5, §6 point 3, §8; DECISIONS.md D-100 points 4 and 9
// (amends D-46 point 4); invariant TR-6.
// Contract: contracts/contracts/primes_lp_sink.tolk.
// Opcodes: shared/opcodes.ts `LP_SINK`.
//
// DeDust PRIMES/GRAM LP receipts are transferred to this contract's own LP
// jetton wallet and are never seen again. One bootstrap, one deposit handler,
// two counters.
//
// THE PROPERTY THIS SCHEMA IS SHORT BECAUSE OF: there is NO OUTBOUND SECTION
// below, and its absence is not an omission. The contract declares no outbound
// message type at all — stronger than "no withdraw path", because there is no
// send to audit. `LpSink.spec.ts` asserts the compiled code cell contains no
// `SENDRAWMSG`. Anything that ever moves this LP is a different contract at a
// different address holding none of this one's balance.
//
// TR-6, THE ONE-LINE AUDIT: `getLocked()` is monotone non-decreasing — one `+=`
// in the whole contract, no `-=` anywhere — and equals the sink's LP jetton
// wallet balance. Two numbers, one comparison.
//
// LOCKED DEPTH IS NEVER SUMMED INTO `T`. A COPY CONSTRAINT, NOT A COMMENT
// (D-100 point 4), and it binds every surface that reads this schema. An LP
// receipt is a claim on a pool whose GRAM/PRIMES composition moves with every
// trade, so any figure derived from it is non-monotonic; `T` is the ratchet's
// GRAM side and §5's theorem is that `p_f = T/S` only ever rises. THE FLOOR
// (redemption ratio, monotone) and LIQUIDITY (locked forever here / committed
// >= 30 d in custody / withdrawable in custody) are two guarantees on two
// panels. No UI string, API field or doc line may present locked depth as
// backing, as collateral, or as part of `T`. What it is: this much of the pair
// can never be pulled.
//
// WHY A SINK AND NOT A TEP-74 BURN OF THE RECEIPT (D-100's "options not
// taken"): a burn is equally permanent and NOT READABLE — turning a drop in the
// LP jetton's supply into "depth locked forever" needs a baseline somebody
// maintains and an argument that no other burner exists. A sink's locked depth
// IS its wallet balance, at any block, with no trusted counter.
//
// §3.4: this contract declares ZERO GRAM liability — absent, not zero-valued —
// so it appears in no reconciliation row and exposes no `getSolvency`. GRAM sent
// here is likewise unrecoverable; it is rent, not a liability. `S` (§3.3) and
// the five-way split (§4.1) are untouched: no opcode here is one the ledger, the
// ratchet or the splitter recognises.
//
// LP locked here is OUT of the electorate (D-100 point 9; D-168 deleted the
// miner): it is computed over `primes_treasury.tolk` custody positions, and this
// contract holds none. A surface offering the "lock forever" button must say so.
// ===========================================================================

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Storage — five fields, one cell, no dictionary and there will not be one.
// WHO deposited is deliberately not recorded: a per-depositor tally would be a
// claim ledger for a claim that can never be made, and it would grow against
// config 43's 65,536-cell account ceiling for no reader's benefit. The
// depositor is on chain in the transfer that brought the tokens.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

lp_sink_storage$_
    // TR-6. Cumulative LP received, in the LP jetton's own units. Written by
    // exactly one statement, which adds a non-negative amount.
    locked:Coins
    events:uint32
    // the sink's OWN DeDust LP jetton wallet — circular-address bootstrap
    // (the D21 family), set one-shot by the genesis script
    lp_jetton_wallet_addr:MsgAddress
    wallet_set:uint8
    // the only sender a `set_wallet` is accepted from. NOT an owner: it names
    // the wallet once and has no privilege afterwards, because no message here
    // does anything else.
    genesis_script_addr:MsgAddress
  = LpSinkStorage;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Inbound
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// one-shot, genesis script only. Refused after the first (error 104), refused
// from anyone else (error 100).
set_wallet#97000001
    query_id:uint64
    lp_jetton_wallet_addr:MsgAddress
  = InternalMsgBody;

// from the sink's OWN LP jetton wallet, and only from it: LP arriving, forever.
//   * before the bootstrap  -> error 1170 lp_sink_wallet_unset
//   * from any other sender -> error 1171 lp_sink_wrong_wallet
//
// The sender check protects the NUMBER, not the money: a forged notification
// can extract nothing from a contract that cannot send, but it could inflate a
// figure a public panel presents as locked depth. Same reasoning as the
// ratchet's burn tally, where behaviour is indifferent to a forgery and only
// the count discriminates.
//
// `forward_payload` KEEPS ITS TEP-74 `(Either Cell ^Cell)` SHAPE AND IS NEVER
// READ, and the difference from sink.tlb's ref-typed field matters: that sink
// is notified by primes_jetton_wallet.tolk, which always writes a ref. This one
// is notified by a DEDUST-ISSUED wallet carrying a payload a stranger composed,
// and a short payload rides INLINE. Insisting on a ref would make such a
// deposit fail to parse — a self-inflicted denial of service in the one
// contract whose only job is to accept LP. The contract consumes the tail as an
// opaque remainder and no branch reads it: there is exactly one thing it can do
// with a deposit, so there is nothing for a payload to select.
transfer_notification#7362d09c
    query_id:uint64
    amount:Coins
    sender:MsgAddress
    forward_payload:(Either Cell ^Cell)
  = InternalMsgBody;

// Any other opcode -> error 101 wrong_opcode. An EMPTY body is accepted: it is
// how the contract is deployed and how anyone tops up its storage rent, and
// that GRAM can no more leave than the LP can.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Outbound
//
// NONE. This section is empty on purpose and must stay empty — see the header.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Get-methods
//
//   getLocked()        -> cumulative LP locked forever, in the LP jetton's own
//                         units. Monotone non-decreasing; equals the sink's LP
//                         jetton wallet balance (TR-6). NOT part of `T`.
//   getEvents()        -> how many separate locks make it up
//   getLpSinkConfig()  -> (lp_jetton_wallet_addr, wallet_set,
//                          genesis_script_addr) — published so `getLocked()`'s
//                         claim is checkable: a reader needs to know WHICH
//                         wallet balance to compare against, and whether the
//                         one-shot has fired.
//
// THERE IS DELIBERATELY NO `getSolvency`, for sink.tlb's reason: the declared
// GRAM liability is ABSENT rather than zero-valued, and a zero row would invite
// a future reader to add it to the §3.4 aggregate.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
